   "text": {
    "L1": "Sleep, play and feelings all help us live well.",
    "L2": "Children need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep each night.",
    "L3": "Sleep helps the body grow, the brain remember learning and us feel fresh.",
    "L4": "Playing and exercising for about an hour each day keeps the body strong and the mind happy.",
    "L5": "We can feel happy, sad, angry, scared or worried. Every feeling is normal, and feelings pass.",
    "L6": "MYTH: Feeling sad means something is wrong with you. NOT TRUE—talking to someone we trust can help us feel better.",
    "L7": "Aarav can play after school, do homework before dinner, turn screens off by 7:30 and sleep by 8:30.",
    "L8": "Now tap the true idea about feelings."
   },
